course: dictionary
lesson: 1639
title: Childish: silly or just young?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Childish is an adjective, so it describes a person, a behaviour or a thing. It can be a criticism, meaning silly or immature, like a small child's. «Don't be childish!» tells someone to act their age.
explain: It can also just describe. «Childish handwriting» means handwriting like a young child's, with no blame. The context tells you which meaning is meant: a person who sulks is being criticised, but the handwriting is only described.
explain: Look for the clues around the word. «"Toot" is a childish, joking word for a fart.» The word joking shows that childish here means playful and young, not nasty. Childlike is the positive word for the same idea, so the context decides whether childish is a compliment or a complaint.
fact: Childish is an adjective: childish, more childish, most childish.
fact: «Don't be childish!» tells someone to act their age. It criticises silly behaviour, sulking or tantrums.
fact: «Childish handwriting» means handwriting like a young child's, said without blame.
fact: «pìgu» means bottom; it is a childish word, not a rude one.
fact: Childlike is always positive, but childish can be a criticism.
exercise: «Don't be childish!» What does this tell someone to do? | *Act their age | Speak more quietly | Go to bed early | Sing a song
exercise: «"Toot" is a childish, joking word for a fart.» What does childish mean here? | Very long and difficult | Old and serious | Rude and dangerous | *Playful and young, like a small child's word
exercise: Which word is the positive one, meaning like a young child without blame? | silly | childish | immature | *childlike
test: «pìgu» means bottom; it is a childish word, not a rude one. What is pìgu? | A playground game | Mouth | *Bottom or bum, a childish word | A rude word for bottom
test: Jayden says childish always means bad. Is he right? | Yes, it always means silly and bad | No, it means old and wise | Yes, but only for adults | *No, it can just describe something like a young child, without blame
exam: Which use of childish is a criticism? | «"Toot" is a childish, joking word» | *Sulking over losing a game, you're being childish | None of these | «Childish handwriting» on the card
